From: libpldm portable build maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] headers: Preserve C++ linkage for standard includes

Developed against upstream be4f63e36408921e76d868593176377de84e945e,
after patches 1-4 in this series.

Public headers such as base.h include pldm_types.h inside extern "C".
When cstddef is first included there, libc++'s templates inherit C
linkage and fail to compile. The responder unit test exposes this on
both macOS architectures because it includes responder.c before any
C++ standard headers.

Give the C++ standard includes their own language-linkage scope. This
also handles consumers wrapping a public C header in extern "C". The
enclosing C linkage is restored afterwards, preserving C entry points
and wire types. Keep the responder test enabled and unchanged.

diff --git a/include/libpldm/pldm_types.h b/include/libpldm/pldm_types.h
--- a/include/libpldm/pldm_types.h
+++ b/include/libpldm/pldm_types.h
@@ -2,8 +2,10 @@
 #pragma once
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C++" {
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <cstddef>
+}
 #else
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
